{
  "screens": [
    {
      "kind": "hookText",
      "text": "Gregor Mendel crossed purple and white pea plants and counted thousands of seeds. The white flowers came back in neat, steady proportions. How could chance give such neat results?",
      "image": null,
      "visual": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "explanation",
      "title": "Each parent passes one copy",
      "text": "Each plant has two copies of the gene, one from each parent. Each copy is an **allele**. P (purple) beats p (white), so one P makes a plant purple. Only pp is white. A Pp × pp cross gives Pp or pp, half the time each.",
      "exampleLineIdea": "A trait you share with a parent, such as eye color or a widow's peak.",
      "image": null,
      "visual": null,
      "explore": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "activity",
      "template": "combinationGrid",
      "content": "{\"template\":\"combinationGrid\",\"prompt\":\"This grid is called a **Punnett square**. Fill each box with the two alleles one offspring can get, one from each parent.\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Pp × pp cross\",\"rule\":\"alleles\",\"columns\":{\"label\":\"White parent (pp)\",\"values\":[\"p\",\"p\"]},\"rows\":{\"label\":\"Purple parent (Pp)\",\"values\":[\"P\",\"p\"]},\"traits\":{\"dominant\":\"purple\",\"recessive\":\"white\"}},\"check\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"question\":\"Out of the four boxes you filled, what share show white?\",\"output\":\"recessive\",\"inputs\":[],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"1 in 4\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"1 in 4 is the share from crossing two Pp plants. This cross has a white pp parent, so count the boxes again.\",\"value\":0.25},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"1 in 2\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"reason\":\"Two of the four boxes are pp, and only pp is white, so 2 out of 4 is 1 in 2.\",\"value\":0.5},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"3 in 4\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Only pp shows white, and that is two of the four boxes, not three.\",\"value\":0.75},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"All of them\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"The Pp boxes are purple, so not all seeds are white.\",\"value\":1}]}}"
    },
    {
      "kind": "activity",
      "template": "randomSimulation",
      "content": "{\"template\":\"randomSimulation\",\"prompt\":\"Guess first: how often will a batch of 100 seeds show exactly 50 white flowers? Then run many batches and check.\",\"fields\":{\"mode\":\"chance\",\"hitLabel\":\"White flowers\",\"trialLabel\":\"seed\",\"runs\":1000,\"model\":{\"kind\":\"binomial\",\"trials\":100,\"probability\":0.5,\"hit\":{\"comparison\":\"exactly\",\"value\":50}}},\"check\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"question\":\"After running many batches, how often did a batch show exactly 50 white flowers?\",\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Most of the time\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Batches land near 50, but exactly 50 is only one of many possible counts, so it comes up far less often.\",\"value\":0.7},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"About half the time\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Half the seeds are white on average, but a batch rarely lands exactly on that count.\",\"value\":0.5},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"About 8% of the time\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"reason\":\"Exactly 50 is one of many possible counts, so a batch lands on it about 8% of the time and lands a little above or below 50 the rest of the time.\",\"value\":0.08},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Almost never\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"reason\":\"Exactly 50 does come up, about 1 batch in 12, so it is not almost never.\",\"value\":0.01}]}}"
    },
    {
      "kind": "check",
      "context": "Keisha, a gardener in Sacramento, plants 100 seeds from a Pp × pp cross. She expects half to be white. Only 47 are white.",
      "question": "Did the 1 in 2 prediction turn out wrong?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, 47 is below 50, so the 1 in 2 prediction was wrong.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "A batch rarely lands exactly on the expected count. Coming in a few under 50 is normal chance spread.",
          "picture": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No, 47 is close to 50, and chance spreads results around the expected 50.",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "reason": "A single batch can miss the expected count by a little. 47 is a small miss, so it doesn't disprove the prediction.",
          "picture": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes, a Pp × pp cross should always give exactly 50 white flowers.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "Chance means one batch can land on a count other than 50, so this cross never promises exactly 50.",
          "picture": null
        }
      ],
      "image": null,
      "visual": null,
      "basis": null
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "ideas": [
      {
        "label": "Punnett square grid",
        "text": "A Punnett square lists every pairing of two parents' alleles, so the share of boxes with a trait gives its chance."
      },
      {
